4. 🍕 Pizza for one
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 Photo courtesy of Domino's


 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A pizza by its nature is meant to be shared. That's no longer good for business, according to Domino's.

 The country's largest pizza chain is introducing the Domino, a pizza specifically marketed as "made for one," Axios' Pete Gannon writes. Zoom in: Domino's says the new offering fills a gap in its portfolio, and caters to the demands of today's "modern pizza occasion."

 It addresses two trends: 👤 More and more people in the U.S. are eating alone, per WSJ , with over 4 in 10 food-service meals eaten solo over the last 12 months through June. 🙅 Even when people are eating as a group they want their own food, Domino's says, a finding gleaned from thousands of interviews it conducted over the last two years. 🤝 Between the lines: Ordering a large pizza is a negotiation, too often requiring compromise and sacrifice, the chain found — a reality that drives would-be customers to burgers and burritos.


 
 
